WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.880
A London room in the 1860s.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.780
A curtain, a chair, and
a window onto the street.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.820
Outside, the houses
opposite run in one long,

4
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.780
flat wall, under a smoky, yellow-grey sky.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.550
People hurry past, eyes down.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.510
Closed carriages roll by, all alike.

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.940
Nobody stops.

8
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.960
A busy city street.

9
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.000
So what is missing from this view?

10
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll meet George Eliot,

11
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.140
the pen name of Mary Ann Evans.

12
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.110
This poem waited until
1959 to be published.

13
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.860
You'll look at the street through
the speaker's eyes, from indoors.

14
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.540
And you'll see why the poem is
one unbroken block of 19 lines.

15
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.690
Your mission: find out
what is missing from it.
